From 642a4b97a115febf3694d3ef94397f061e2917ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:52:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: cpr3: Fix the probe error path loop

The genpd cleanup loop of cpr_probe() counts down an unsigned index
while it is not negative, so any error after the threads are initialised
(for example a deferred reference clock) never ends the loop and removes
domains past the start of the thread array. Use a signed index.

Scope: SDM630/660 common
Porting notes: Local fix for the CPR3 driver (not upstream).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr3.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr3.c b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr3.c
index fdfe13bbbd..65e0be9b42 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr3.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr3.c
@@ -2531,8 +2531,7 @@ static int cpr_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	const struct cpr_desc *desc;
 	const struct cpr_acc_desc *data;
 	struct device_node *np;
-	unsigned int i;
-	int ret;
+	int i, ret;
 
 	data = of_device_get_match_data(dev);
 	if (!data || !data->cpr_desc)
